Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:14.310 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hey there anime fans if you're here  chances are that you've already watched  my video of the top 10 badass moments in  one piece  and if you enjoyed that then you know  why you're here again because it's time  for volume 2.  why well why not one piece is full of  such brilliant moments of  courage spunk attitude and general  badassery  that it just makes sense to make a  second list in this video you're going  to find both one-on-one encounters and  one versus many fights stylish entrances  and moments of quiet strength where  battles are won without raising a weapon  there are moments where the hero doesn't  win for a change and where the villain  shows  why he's the top boss naturally there  are spoilers ahead  at number 10 it's luffy finishing off  rob lucci  after a hard-fought battle that almost  didn't go the straw hat captain's way  the final showdown between the pirate  and the cp-9 agent takes place at the  end of the enemy's lobby arc  which stands out as an emotional arc  that served to cement the deep bond  between the straw hats  luci has the upper hand against luffy  for most of the battle at one moment  it seems luffy's out for the count and  robin's chance of happiness is all but  dashed but usopp's strong words of  encouragement pushed luffy to tap into  hidden reserves of resistance  and stand up to his enemy one last time  it's just enough to get the job done  and it reminds us yet again of luffy's  tenacity and his aversion  to giving up against a stronger opponent  this next moment on our list is all  style and panache as sanji living up to  himself given name of mr prince makes a  timely entrance at crocodile's base to  save his crewmates  luffy and gang are in all kinds of  trouble locked up in a sea stone cage in  a croc infested room that's flooding  fast the key to the cage lies in the  stomach of one very snappy bananawani  using his guile and cunning sanji tricks  crocodile into leaving his base  he then breaks into the flooded room and  with a powerful kick that sends  one gigantic croc out of his way saves  the day  as for sanji's mr prince monika well  surely you would have caught on by now  it's a clever bit of foreshadowing by  the mangaka echiro  oda a not so subtle hint to the  revelation many many arcs later that  sanji's actually a prince of the  vinsmoke family  [Music]  up next is luffy challenging big mom a  second time  before they meet in person the first two  interactions between the upstart and the  yonko are telephonic  during their first exchange at the end  of the fishman island arc  luffy fresh off a big win tells big mom  on the den then mushi that he's not only  eaten all her candy but that he plans to  kick her ass all over the new world  unlike this spur-of-the-moment  provocation his second challenge to her  is more personal and more hostile  imprisoned on whole cake island and  unable to rescue sanji  luffy's in a desperate situation yet he  shows his captain  no fear what's more he treats her with  disdain naturally this infuriates big  one to no end but that's exactly  what luffy wants this time his  declaration of war conveys not the boast  of a kid riding high on a win  but the conviction of a man who knows  what he wants and won't let  anything or anybody get in his way even  if it's the most powerful woman  in the world  [Music]  coming in at number seven is luffy's one  punch takedown of  bellamy  in search of the sky island of skypier  the straw hats arrive in jaya there they  run into bellamy the hyena a  rabble-rousing rookie  before his character development in the  dress roster arc bellamy is a rather  unlikable character  he bullies the weak he's arrogant and  he's full of himself too he runs with a  nasty crew  he taunts and humiliates luffy and zorro  for no good reason but what really puts  him at odds with luffy  is that he doesn't believe in dreams  amongst those who do to him  anybody who believes that skypier and  his city of gold exists  is a fool unfortunately though for  bellamy he also seriously underestimates  luffy taking him for a weakling and his  unwillingness to fight as a sign  of cowardice which earns him a punishing  punch to the face from luffy it's always  satisfying to see a bully get what he  deserves isn't it  the shonen fandom loves a superhero who  can single-handedly fight an entire army  zorro happens to be one such hero when  he's not lost and wondering about the  swordsman of the straw hat pirates can  be an extremely capable  first mate to his captain and crew we  saw his incredible loyalty and  sacrificing heart in the incident with  bartholomew kumar which made our first  list of badass moments but  even before that zoro showed us this  side of his character in whiskey peak  when he single-handedly defeated 100  bounty hunters  including a few of crocodile's top  officers and saved his sleeping  crewmates from their evil designs  his sword skills are enough to confuse  his opponents into thinking he's the  real captain of the crew now that he  treats the fight not as a life and death  situation but as an opportunity to test  out his newly acquired swords  makes him such a badass in our books  we're at the halfway mark now and we  have kizaru making short work of the  supernovas  the star body arc makes an important  turning point in the straw hat's journey  it's where luffy famously punches a  celestial dragon  another moment that made it to our first  list another reason that this makes this  arc significant is that it serves as an  introduction to the supernovas the 11  top  rookie pirates perceived as the next big  threat to the world government their  arrival in sambodi at the same time and  luffy's antics at the slave auction  cause such a stir  that it puts them on a direct collision  course with the marines their army of  pacifistas and admiral kizuru however as  brash and fearless as the rookies are  they soon realize they're no match for  the slow speaking  lightning fast admiral kizuru easily  defeats hawkins  drake apple and urug while the straw  hats escape his wrath only with  rayleigh's timely help kizuru may not be  antagonistic like akainu or aokiji but  he makes for a fascinating and often  unpredictable character  [Music]  next up is sabo revealing his special  technique  dragon's breath you talking  taken for dead after he drowned as a  child luffy's sworn brother returns  during the corridor coliseum tournament  in the dress roster arc  taking luffy's place in the fight he  goes up against such big-name opponents  as diamante and burgess disarming both  of them easily with his unique  dragon claw fist martial arts while  showing the same irreverent and  fun-loving fighting style as his brash  younger brother but it's his display of  dragon's breath that's  truly awe-inspiring imbuing his clenched  fists with haki and punching them into  the ground  sarvo sends a shock wave so great that  he completely destroys the arena  sending his opponents in the audience  floundering it is indeed a worthy  exhibition of power for the second in  command of the revolutionary army and  the man chosen to inherit fire fist  ace's devil fruit powers  [Music]  big mom sake cup this is a quiet moment  of courage that's as powerful  as the flashiest showdown with her  unpredictable temperament and  uncontrollable hunger pangs  big mom's one of the most terrifying  forces in one piece  imagine standing up to her at a time  when her best laid plans are falling  apart and she's ready to lose it  jinbe not only dares to do just that but  gets away with it too as luffy and gang  gay crash the grand wedding on whole  cake island  jinbei once again states his intention  to leave big mom's crew and join the  straw hats the furious yonko intends to  make him pay with his life  but shockingly fails to do so because  the fish man shows absolutely no fear of  her and her powers now this  is an incredibly powerful scene made all  the better with the drama and the  dialogue it just goes to show that there  are a few characters as loyal and strong  as the gentle jinbe  esta  in the runner-up spot we have kaido  one-shotting luffy in their very first  encounter in the wano arc  now we've always known that luffy  doesn't think much about picking a fight  with a bigger  stronger meaner opponent he's done it  before and he does it as soon as he  lands in the land of the samurai where  he's supposed to be keeping a low  profile now while luffy does lend a few  lucky hits on the punch drunk yonko by  going all  out we know he's horribly out of his  league there's just no way he can defeat  the man who can't be killed even by  himself right so it's really no surprise  when kaido sobers up just enough to  knock luffy out with one  devastating smack of his black thunder  club the captain of the straw hats is  out for the count despite being in his  armament haki enhanced gear fourth bound  man form that's just how  crazy dangerous kaido is with the wano  story still unfolding its mysteries we  can't help but wonder if luffy's  actually up to the task of bringing down  the invincible yonko  here  [Music]  and that brings us to number one and  taking the top spot is the post time  skip  monster trio turning the lethal pacifist  into heavy metal trash  since their separation at the hands of  bartholomew kumar two years ago the  straw hats have been on their own  training and powering up so they can  reunite one day and resume their journey  acquire reunions out of the question at  least for luffy  zorro and sanji when the monster trio  meet again it's naturally with the  marines and the pacifistas hot on their  heels  the weaponized cyborgs have given the  straw hats endless trouble  two years ago but this time they're more  prepared for them this scene may not  have the gravitas of a serious battle  it is in fact comical in tone with luffy  lugging around a giant backpack filled  with food yet the display of their  newfound strength and growth in  abilities  still makes for a very special moment  it's the monster trio we've loved  and missed after all only stronger and  better than before  and that's it folks given how full of  meaningful and impactful moments this  series is  we might be able to make a volume three  or even a volume four wouldn't that be  great so if you enjoyed this video give  it a like and let me know  well for the time being i hope you  enjoyed volume two tell me if some of  your favorite moments made it to the  list  you can also drop me a line about any  moment you think should have been on  this list i'd love to hear from you you  can subscribe to vinichu for more top  10s and anime content  and i'll see you in the next video  it

